# Cooler LCD panel (HID 5131:2007).
#
# The node is granted to a dedicated system group rather than to every logged-in
# user, so only the service (which runs with SupplementaryGroups=cooler-lcd)
# can drive the panel.
#
# The file name matters. TAG+="uaccess" only marks the device; the ACL is
# granted by the uaccess builtin, which runs from RUN{builtin}+ in
# 73-seat-late.rules. A rule numbered above 73 still gets its tag applied, but
# the step that consumes the tag has already run, so no ACL appears. This must
# therefore sort before 73, and after 50-udev-default.rules so these MODE/GROUP
# values win over that file's defaults.
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="5131", ATTRS{idProduct}=="2007", MODE="0660", GROUP="@GROUP@"
